.alert.alert-light.border
  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Goal of this page
  %p.mb-3
    Replace spreadsheet MAAP feedback with structured suggestion rounds so managers can comment on Assignments and propose Ability milestones — without granting MAAP edit access.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Context
  = render "shared/maap/definition"
  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 What a well-oiled MAAP looks like
  %ol.mb-3
    %li.mb-2
      %strong Assignments first.
      Break job descriptions into Assignments with clear outcomes (often 2 for early-career roles, up to ~10 for later-career; more than 10 usually signals trouble).
      You will know this is working when manager and employee rate the same ~80% of the time, ratings distribute across working-to-meet / meeting / exceeding (meeting &gt; 50%, each other &gt; 5%), and every Assignment has observations across all four observation ratings.
    %li.mb-2
      %strong Then Abilities.
      For each Assignment, define 2–10 Abilities (skills, knowledge, behaviors) and set milestones (often M1/M2, rarely M3; M4–M5 on an Assignment is usually inappropriate).
      You will know this is working when milestones are awarded, goals attach to needed milestones, and every Ability has observations across all four observation ratings.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Specifics of this page
  %ul.mb-3
    %li One open suggestion round per Position. First joiner opens it; a MAAP manager closes it. A later joiner can open a new round after close. Rounds support the MAAP cadence of revisiting each position regularly (ideally at least every six months).
    %li Comments are person-scoped inside the round (visible to anyone using this UI). Suggested Assignment–Ability milestones are shared on the round bag, with who last changed them and PaperTrail history.
    %li
      %strong Done making suggestions
      clears your personal queue — it does not accept changes into MAAP.
    %li Milestone suggestions are proposals only in this beta; MAAP managers apply real milestone changes elsewhere (Accept/Reject coming soon).
    %li
      Completing a round requires no unresolved
      %em root
      comments from active (non-withdrawn) participants — including ability-milestone suggestion threads (resolving that comment is how a milestone suggestion is marked handled). Replies do not need individual resolve.
